{
  "meta": {
    "name": "Effects tour: compositing and light",
    "description": "Chapter 5 of the effects tour: section layouts with bundled photographs (a three-pane horizontal split with gaps, a stacked vertical split with a divider, a before/after wipe), then every fx primitive (graphics[].type \"fx\") in its family: light (sheen, edge-glow, leak, bloom), marks (ripple, glint, confetti), ambient (bokeh, dust, vignette-breathe, grain) and surfaces (glass, resolve).",
    "creativeDirection": "Comparison as composition, then light as material: the triptych names its shores on a backing panel, the stacked pair labels each pane on its own side, and the wipe uncovers the tidy desk. Each fx beat shows one primitive anchored to what it decorates (a card, a button, a title, the photo) and tuned for it. Review: panes stay cover-fitted, dividers are crisp, light never greys or floats outside its target, ambient textures stay faint, and type never straddles a pane boundary."
  },
